hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17720","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Qays, from Dukayn ibn Said al-Muzani who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), forty riders and four hundred, asking him for food. He said to Umar: Go and give them. He said: O Messenger of Allah, nothing remains but some sas of dates which I do not think will sustain me. He said: Go and give them. He said: Hearing and obeying. He said: Umar took the key out of his waist wrapper and opened the door, and there was something like a reclining young camel of dates. He said: Let you take. Each man among us took what he liked. Then I turned, while I was among the last of the people, and it was as if we had taken not a date."
"17721","Waki narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Qays, from Dukayn ibn Said al-Khathami who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while we were four hundred and forty. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"17722","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Qays, from Dukayn ibn Said who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he mentioned the hadith."
"17723","Yala and Muhammad, the two sons of Ubayd, narrated to us, both saying: Ismail narrated to us, from Qays, from Dukayn ibn Said al-Muzani who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he mentioned the hadith."
